introduction
	The main window icons provide quick and easy \
	access to useful interface commands.  \
	Each icon has an equivalent menu command.
	
	The descriptions below contain the sequence of \
	menu selections to perform the same function as \
	the icon button.\

delete
	Delete the selected widgets.\
delete menu
	Edit, Delete\

hide
	Hide (unmap) the selected widgets.\
hide menu
	View, Hide, Selection\

raise
	Raise the selected widgets.\
raise menu
	View, Raise\

lower
	Lower the selected widgets.\
lower menu
	View, Lower\

cut
	Remove the selected widgets and save them in the cut buffer.\
cut menu
	View, Cut\

copy
	Copy the selected widgets into the cut\
	buffer.\
copy menu
	View, Copy\

paste
	Paste the contents of the cut buffer.\
paste menu
	View, Paste\

list
	Toggle the widget list.  If it is hidden, show it.  \
	If it is shown, hide it, then show the widget tree \
	if it was not visible.\
list menu
	Windows, Widget List\

tree
	Toggle the widget tree.  If it is hidden, show it.  \
	If it is shown, hide it, then show the widget list \
	if it was not visible.\
tree menu
	Windows, Widget Tree\

track
	Select a widget with the mouse, and place \
	its fully-qualified name into the text cut buffer.\
track menu
	Edit, Track\

expand
	Expand the selected widgets in the widget list and the widget tree.\
expand menu
	View, Expand\

shrink
	Shrink the selected widgets in the widget list and the widget tree.\
shrink menu
	View, Shrink\

print tree
	Print the widget tree to a PostScript file.\
print tree menu
	File, Print, Tree\
no print tree
	The Print Tree icon takes this form when the widget \
	tree is not visible.\

print window
	Select a window to print to a PostScript file.\
print window menu
	File, Print, Window\

reslist introduction
	For every resource in the resource list, an icon \
	indicates if the resource has been modified by the user, \
	and if so how it will be saved in the interface files.
	The icon is located between the resource name and the \
	resource value. \
	\
	If the `Use Fast Resource List' option is set, \
	the icons are replaced by characters in square brackets. \
	The character corresponding to each icon is shown in \
	this window after the explanation text.

resdflt
	This resource has not been modified, and its default \
	value can be displayed as a character string.
resdflt char
	[d]

resnone
	This resource has not been modified, and its default \
	value cannot be displayed as a character string.
resnone char
	[-]

resset
	This resource has been modified by the user. Its value \
	will be saved in the .fm file, so it cannot be modified \
	by the end-user of the application.
resset char
	[S]

resrdb
	This resource has been modified by the user. Its value \
	will be saved in a resource file (.rdb), so it can be \
	overriden by the end-user of the application.
resrdb char
	[R]

restmpl
	This resource is inherited from a template and has not \
	been modified. It will not be saved in the .fm file \
	containing this widget, but only in the template file.
restmpl char
	[T]
